## Summary

Extract common terminal graphics patterns from terminal-stars into a reusable library that can be shared across jcaldwell-labs C projects (tario, adventure-engine-v2, boxes-live, atari-style).

## Shared Patterns Identified

### 1. Frame Buffer
```c
typedef struct {
    char *buffer;
    int *colors;
    int width, height;
} FrameBuffer;

FrameBuffer *framebuffer_create(int w, int h);
void framebuffer_clear(FrameBuffer *fb);
void framebuffer_display(FrameBuffer *fb);
void framebuffer_destroy(FrameBuffer *fb);
```

### 2. Terminal Abstraction
```c
bool terminal_init(void);
void terminal_cleanup(void);
void terminal_get_size(int *w, int *h);
void terminal_handle_resize(void);
```

### 3. Delta-Time
```c
double get_delta_time(void);  // Returns seconds since last call
```

### 4. Color Utilities
```c
void color_init_pairs(void);
int color_from_depth(double z, double max_z);
```

## Proposed Library: termgfx

```
termgfx/
├── include/
│   ├── termgfx.h      # Main header
│   ├── framebuffer.h
│   ├── terminal.h
│   └── timing.h
├── src/
│   ├── framebuffer.c
│   ├── terminal.c
│   └── timing.c
└── Makefile
```

## Benefits

- DRY across 5+ projects
- Tested patterns in one place
- Easier onboarding to any project
- Consistent terminal behavior

## Integration

Projects would use:
```makefile
LDFLAGS += -ltermgfx
```

Or git submodule for single-binary distribution.
EOF
