  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary

Create a WASM build of terminal-stars that runs in the browser using xterm.js. This eliminates installation friction and enables instant demos.

## Technical Approach

### 1. Emscripten Build

Replace ncurses with a minimal terminal abstraction:
```c
#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
#include <emscripten.h>
// Use EM_ASM for terminal output
#else
#include <ncurses.h>
#endif
```

### 2. xterm.js Frontend

```html
<div id="terminal"></div>
<script src="xterm.js"></script>
<script>
  const term = new Terminal();
  term.open(document.getElementById('terminal'));
  
  Module.print = (text) => term.write(text);
  Module.printErr = (text) => console.error(text);
</script>
```

### 3. Build Command

```makefile
wasm:
    emcc src/*.c -o docs/terminal-stars.js \
        -s WASM=1 \
        -s EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS='["_main"]' \
        --shell-file shell.html
```

